# Branch from main before work

Before implementation on a change that will become a commit or MR:

1. `git fetch` the GitLab remote and update local `main`.
2. Create and check out a new branch from that tip.
3. Do the work on that branch — not on `main`, and not by continuing an
   unrelated leftover branch unless the operator named it.

Skip only for pure questions, plan-only turns, or when the operator
already named the branch to use.
